  set:  # 6f7a
    title: "scala.io.StdIn.readLine is catalogued ipc_recv but unreachable in its FULLY-QUALIFIED inline form: emitted as a hint-less ambiguous short name (imported forms reach)"  # 6f7a
    fields:  # 6f7a
      statement: "A scala.io.StdIn stdin reader must reach its ipc_recv catalogue entry in every call form. VIOLATED for the FULLY-QUALIFIED inline form only: scala.io.StdIn.readLine() is emitted as scala:external:0-0:readLine with no module slot, and readLine is in scala's ambiguous_names, so the no-module gate withholds it. The imported forms (import scala.io.StdIn; StdIn.readLine() and import scala.io.StdIn.readLine; readLine()) reach the row (re-verified 2026-09-27)."  # 6f7a
      root_cause: "The scala analyzer does not put the package path of a fully-qualified call expression (a.b.C.f(...) with no import) into the module slot, so it is indistinguishable from a bare ambiguous readLine and is correctly withheld for lack of evidence. Not specific to StdIn: scala.sys.process.Process(s).run() loses its slot the same way. Imported and import-qualified receivers are resolved (re-verified 2026-09-27)."  # 6f7a
- op: discuss  # 72e0
  at: '2026-09-28T02:03:04Z'  # 72e0
  by: agent  # 72e0
