  nonce: '72e0'  # 72e0
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-27 at dev f474411e11. STILL VIOLATED, but NARROWER than filed: statement, root_cause and title re-scoped to the one form that is still withheld.\n\nShipped CLI (survey + io-boundaries, cold cache):\n  val s = scala.io.StdIn.readLine()            -> scala:external:0-0:readLine, call_construct=method, no module slot; WITHHELD, no chain   (the filed repro; still fails)\n  import scala.io.StdIn; StdIn.readLine()      -> scala:scala.io.StdIn:0-0:readLine -> ipc_recv chain                                        (REACHES)\n  import scala.io.StdIn.readLine; readLine()   -> scala:scala.io.StdIn.readLine:0-0:readLine -> ipc_recv chain                               (REACHES)\n\nThe item's measurement (vutav_reads_08302026/reach/scala/M.scala) used ONLY the fully-qualified inline form, so it never showed whether the imported forms reached; I cannot say whether they were fixed after 09-03 (candidates: WI-tipoh 9e8ed17fca, WI-kilap d5f8060a45) or always worked. What is established is that today only the fully-qualified call expression is lost.\n\nSAME MECHANISM, SECOND SYMPTOM on the same fixture line: scala.sys.process.Process(s).run() emits scala:external:0-0:Process and scala:external:0-0:run, and no subprocess chain. A fully-qualified inline call loses its module slot whatever the callee.\n\nPOPULATION, local corpus (36,524 .scala files): 13 fully-qualified scala.io.StdIn.<x>( calls, 12 StdIn.<x>( calls, 14 imports of scala.io.StdIn; 1 fully-qualified scala.sys.process.Process(. So the still-lost form is about half of the real StdIn uses."  # 72e0
