  message: "Fixed in PR #1267 (fdd99a9eae). The receiver branch now reads a receiver made only of identifiers as a dotted path and, when its root is scala / java / javax and not bound in the file, takes it as the module (WI-pokam's inline-qualification rule, call form). Behavioural evidence on merged dev, the item's own repro 'val s = scala.io.StdIn.readLine(); scala.sys.process.Process(s).run()' through hypergumbo io-boundaries --format json (cold cache): ipc_recv scala.io.StdIn.readLine in Main.full (was withheld: scala:external:0-0:readLine), and subprocess + fs_write scala.sys.process.Process.Process in Main.full (was external, no chain); the two imported forms unchanged. A/B on real repos (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vokut_09282026/): sbt +3 fs_read (Files.exists, Files.readAllBytes, Source.fromInputStream), lila +1 (Source.fromFile), nothing lost. Guards pinned in test_scala_fully_qualified_call.py: a chain on a local value, a third-party root, a member value (scala.Console.err, which the first cut wrongly qualified on sbt) and a file-bound root all keep the sentinel. Residuals, stated: a third-party fully-qualified path (org.x.Y.f()) keeps the sentinel by design; kotlin has the same inline shape and emits NO edge at all, filed as INV-dupol (P2); java already handles it."  # 9861
